cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "QSC Coder: a deterministic content-analysis instrument for Governance-of-Expectations measurement"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, peer-reviewable content-analysis tool that codes policy and
  governance documents against a YAML codebook of twelve sub-codes spanning the
  Expectation Construction (EXP) and Institutionalisation (INST) families, and
  emits per-document Governance-of-Expectations measurements (the EXP/INST
  imbalance score B, a specificity index, a named-standard mention index, an
  EXP-INST co-occurrence matrix, and pipeline-completeness flags). Every run is
  stamped with a cryptographic provenance manifest for independent
  re-execution. No machine-learning component sits in the coding loop.
type: software
